# device-gateway environment configuration template — placeholder only.
# No real secrets. `src/broker_config.py` reads this via `os.environ` directly (this deployable
# has no dotenv/`.env`-file loader, unlike the Business API's pydantic-settings config) — for
# local dev, export these into your shell before running `python -m src.gateway`, e.g.:
#   set -a; . .env; set +a   (bash)   or   Get-Content .env | ... (PowerShell — see README)

# --- Event Broker (Redis Streams, ADR-0008/ADR-0010; hardened Priority 1 Item 4, docs/runbooks/
# --- redis-operations.md) — must match the Business API's own RAAD_BROKER__URL exactly
# --- (backend/.env.example: same password, same db number) so both deployables share the one
# --- `raad:events` stream — a mismatch silently splits them onto two disjoint streams instead of
# --- raising an error. Local dev: docker/docker-compose.yml's `redis` service (ADR-0012), db 1
# --- (not db 0 — that's RAAD_REDIS__URL's cache/rate-limit namespace, kept separate).
# DEVICE_GATEWAY_BROKER_URL=redis://:dev-only-change-me@localhost:6379/1
